// The escaping call site is not promoted; it passes null.
//
// `main` bounds the result of `alloc_and_return`, so the callee gains the trailing
// handle and main's call fills the frame's arena. `pass_through` hands the same
// storage straight back to its own caller, so nothing there can own it: that site
// passes null and the callee allocates from the general allocator for it.
//
// One arena is still created - for main's call - and the callee's branch is what
// keeps pass_through's result out of it.
int* function alloc_and_return() {
    var node = memory.allocate<int>(8);
    node[0] = 42;
    return node;
}

int* function pass_through() {
    return alloc_and_return();
}

int function main() {
    var n = alloc_and_return();
    print(n[0]);
    var m = pass_through();
    print(m[0]);
    return 0;
}
